WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.680
Part 2. You will hear the Chairman of Stanthorpe Twinning Association, which organises the

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:14.240
link between Stanthorpe in England and a town in France, talking to members about the year's

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:20.080
events. First you have some time to look at questions 11 to 15.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:59.439
Now listen carefully and answer questions 11 to 15.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:09.559
It's great to see so many members of the Twinning Association here tonight. Since the

00:01:09.559 --> 00:01:17.040
twinning link between our two towns, Stanthorpe, here in England, and Mallat, in France, was

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:23.919
established, the relationship between the towns has gone from strength to strength.

00:01:23.919 --> 00:01:31.519
Last month, 25 members of the Association from Stanthorpe spent a weekend in Mallat.

00:01:31.519 --> 00:01:38.680
Our hosts had arranged a great programme. We learned how cheese is produced in the region,

00:01:38.680 --> 00:01:45.080
and had the chance to taste the products. The theme park trip had to be cancelled, but

00:01:45.080 --> 00:01:52.800
we all had a great time on the final boat trip down the river, that was the real highlight.

00:01:52.800 --> 00:02:00.519
This is a special year for the Association, because it's 25 years since we were founded.

00:02:00.519 --> 00:02:05.800
In Mallat, they're planning to mark this by building a footbridge in the municipal

00:02:05.800 --> 00:02:13.240
park. We've been discussing what to do here, and we've decided to plant a poplar tree

00:02:13.240 --> 00:02:20.119
in the museum gardens. We considered buying a garden seat to put there, but the authorities

00:02:20.119 --> 00:02:26.880
weren't happy with that idea. In terms of fundraising to support our activities,

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:35.399
we've done very well. Our pancake evening was well attended and made record profits.

00:02:35.399 --> 00:02:42.759
And everyone enjoyed the demonstration of French cookery, which was nearly as successful.

00:02:42.759 --> 00:02:48.559
Numbers for our film show were limited because of the venue, so we're looking for somewhere

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:55.119
bigger next year. We're looking forward to welcoming our French visitors here next

00:02:55.119 --> 00:03:02.559
week, and I know that many of you here will be hosting individuals or families. The coach

00:03:02.559 --> 00:03:10.720
from France will arrive at 5pm on Friday. Don't try to do too much that first evening

00:03:10.720 --> 00:03:18.119
as they'll be tired, so have dinner in the house or garden rather than eating out. The

00:03:18.119 --> 00:03:25.479
weather looks as if it'll be okay, so you might like to plan a barbecue. Then the next

00:03:25.479 --> 00:03:33.080
morning's market day in town, and that's always a good place to stroll round. On Saturday

00:03:33.080 --> 00:03:39.399
evening we'll all meet up at the football club, where once again we'll have Toby Sharp

00:03:39.399 --> 00:03:46.720
and his band performing English and Scottish country songs. Toby will already be well known

00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:53.800
to many of you, as last year he organised our special quiz night and presented the prizes.

00:03:57.199 --> 00:04:03.440
Before you hear the rest of the talk, you have some time to look at questions 16 to 20.

00:04:16.720 --> 00:04:32.720
Now listen and answer questions 16 to 20.

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:43.279
Now, on Sunday we'll be taking our visitors to Farley House. You may not all be familiar

00:04:43.359 --> 00:04:49.200
with it, so here's a map to help you. You can see the car park at the bottom of the

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:55.279
map. There's an excellent farm shop in the grounds, where our visitors can buy local

00:04:55.279 --> 00:05:02.079
produce. It's in the old stables, which is the first building you come to. They're

00:05:02.079 --> 00:05:08.559
built round a courtyard, and the shop's in the far corner on the left. There's also

00:05:08.559 --> 00:05:16.079
a small cafe on the right as you go in. I know that one or two of our visitors may not

00:05:16.079 --> 00:05:23.279
be all that mobile. The main entrance to the house has a lot of steps, so you might want

00:05:23.279 --> 00:05:31.279
to use the disabled entry. This is on the far side of the house from the car park. Children

00:05:31.279 --> 00:05:37.839
will probably be most interested in the Adventure Playground. That's at the northern end of

00:05:37.839 --> 00:05:44.559
the larger lake, in a bend on the path that leads to the lake. There's lots for children

00:05:44.559 --> 00:05:51.839
to do there. There are a number of lovely gardens near the house. The kitchen gardens

00:05:51.839 --> 00:05:58.239
are rectangular and surrounded by a wall. They're to the northeast of the house, quite

00:05:58.239 --> 00:06:06.559
near the smaller lake. They're still in use and have a great collection of fruit and vegetables.

00:06:06.559 --> 00:06:13.279
The Temple of the Four Winds is a bit more of a walk, but it's worth it. Take the path

00:06:13.279 --> 00:06:20.720
from the car park and go past the western sides of the stables and the house. Then,

00:06:20.720 --> 00:06:28.320
when the path forks, take the right-hand path. Go up there with the woods on your left, and

00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:35.600
the Temple is right at the end. There are great views over the whole area. Okay, so

00:06:35.600 --> 00:06:46.640
that's the end of Part 2. You now have 30 seconds to check your answers to Part 2.

00:06:58.320 --> 00:06:58.820
you

